data: {"answer": "This is the **Restaurant POS** room, where orders flow to the kitchen display and cards are paid on encrypted terminals. The most tightly regulated data here is card data, so you must never store CVV or PINs, mask card numbers, and treat unexpected emails with suspicion. You can see systems like the Point of Sale (POS), Card Payment Terminal, Kitchen Display System, and Staff Laptops in this area. Threats displayed include Phishing Emails, POS Memory-Scraping Malware, and Card Skimming/Tampering, while controls visible are P2PE & Tokenization.", "go": [{"key": "bar", "en": "Bar Inventory & ERP", "zh": "酒吧庫存與 ERP", "base_en": "Bar", "base_zh": "酒吧", "url": "https://livetour.istaging.com/6a1e0bab-b805-4788-935b-97a06a024613?index=4", "tour": "A", "why_en": "Next in the story", "why_zh": "故事的下一站"}], "followups": [{"text": "What does the Point of Sale (POS) do?", "en": "What does the Point of Sale (POS) do?", "zh": "餐飲收銀系統（POS）是做什麼的？"}, {"text": "How do we prevent phishing email?", "en": "How do we prevent phishing email?", "zh": "釣魚郵件要怎麼防？"}, {"text": "What should I do next?", "en": "What should I do next?", "zh": "接下來要去哪？"}], "trace": {"session": "offline", "lang": "en", "model": "qwen3.5:9b", "timings": {"route_s": 0.0, "tool_s": 0.02, "answer_s": 18.79, "total_s": 18.86}, "route": {"tool": "room_overview", "target": "", "how": "button"}, "link": {"query": "(current room)", "chosen": "hall", "how": "current room"}, "redirect": "", "queries": [{"purpose": "everything placed in this room", "cypher": "MATCH (r:Room {key:$k}) RETURN r {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .it_en, .it_zh, .tour, .url, .url_index, .area, .kind, .story, .theme_en, .theme_zh, .lesson_en, .lesson_zh} AS r, [(r)-[:IN_AREA]->(a) | a {.key, .name_en, .name_zh}][0] AS area, [(r)-[:CLOSEUP_OF]->(p) | p {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .it_en, .it_zh, .tour, .url, .url_index, .area, .kind, .story, .theme_en, .theme_zh, .lesson_en, .lesson_zh}][0] AS parent, [(s:System)-[:LOCATED_IN]->(r) | s {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .desc_en, .desc_zh}] AS systems, [(t:Threat)-[:SHOWN_IN]->(r) | t {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .desc_en, .desc_zh}] AS threats, [(c:Control)-[:SEEN_IN]->(r) | c {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .desc_en, .desc_zh, .type}] AS controls, [(c:Concept)-[:TAUGHT_IN]->(r) | c {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .desc_en, .desc_zh}] AS concepts, [(p:Procedure)-[:PRACTISED_IN]->(r) | p {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .kind}] AS procedures, [(d:Department)-[:BASED_IN]->(r) | d {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .desc_en, .desc_zh, .ext}] AS departments, [(cs:CaseStudy)-[:SHOWN_IN]->(r) | cs {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .year}] AS cases, [(r)-[l:LINKS_TO]->(x) | x {.key, .name_en, .name_zh, .it_en, .it_zh, .tour, .url, .url_index, .area, .kind, .story, .theme_en, .theme_zh, .lesson_en, .lesson_zh, teleport: l.teleport}] AS exits, size([(f:Finding)-[:IN_ROOM]->(r) | f]) AS findings_here", "params": {"k": "hall"}, "rows": 1, "ms": 23.9}], "graph": {"nodes": [{"key": "hall", "label": "Room", "en": "Restaurant", "zh": "餐廳"}, {"key": "pos", "label": "System", "en": "Point of Sale (POS)", "zh": "餐飲收銀系統（POS）"}, {"key": "pin_pad", "label": "System", "en": "Card Payment Terminal", "zh": "刷卡機"}, {"key": "email", "label": "System", "en": "Email & Collaboration", "zh": "電子郵件與協作平台"}, {"key": "endpoints", "label": "System", "en": "Staff Laptops, PCs & Phones", "zh": "員工筆電、電腦與手機"}, {"key": "kds", "label": "System", "en": "Kitchen Display System", "zh": "廚房出單系統"}, {"key": "phishing", "label": "Threat", "en": "Phishing Email", "zh": "釣魚郵件"}, {"key": "pos_malware", "label": "Threat", "en": "POS Memory-Scraping Malware", "zh": "POS 記憶體側錄惡意程式"}, {"key": "skimming", "label": "Threat", "en": "Card Skimming & Terminal Tampering", "zh": "刷卡機側錄與竄改"}, {"key": "p2pe_tokenization", "label": "Control", "en": "P2PE & Tokenization", "zh": "點對點加密與代碼化"}, {"key": "no_sad_storage", "label": "Control", "en": "Never Store CVV or PIN", "zh": "不儲存安全碼與 PIN"}, {"key": "c_encryption_hashing", "label": "Concept", "en": "Encryption vs Hashing", "zh": "加密與雜湊"}, {"key": "c_pci_scope", "label": "Concept", "en": "Cardholder Data Environment (PCI scope)", "zh": "持卡人資料環境（PCI 範圍）"}, {"key": "c_tokenization", "label": "Concept", "en": "Tokenization", "zh": "代碼化"}], "edges": [{"a": "pos", "t": "SENDS_TO", "b": "kds"}, {"a": "pos", "t": "LOCATED_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "pin_pad", "t": "LOCATED_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "kds", "t": "LOCATED_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "email", "t": "LOCATED_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "endpoints", "t": "LOCATED_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "phishing", "t": "TARGETS", "b": "endpoints"}, {"a": "phishing", "t": "TARGETS", "b": "email"}, {"a": "phishing", "t": "SHOWN_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "pos_malware", "t": "TARGETS", "b": "pos"}, {"a": "pos_malware", "t": "SHOWN_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "skimming", "t": "TARGETS", "b": "pin_pad"}, {"a": "skimming", "t": "SHOWN_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "c_encryption_hashing", "t": "TAUGHT_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "c_encryption_hashing", "t": "RELATED_TO", "b": "p2pe_tokenization"}, {"a": "c_tokenization", "t": "TAUGHT_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "c_tokenization", "t": "RELATED_TO", "b": "p2pe_tokenization"}, {"a": "c_pci_scope", "t": "TAUGHT_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "c_pci_scope", "t": "RELATED_TO", "b": "p2pe_tokenization"}, {"a": "p2pe_tokenization", "t": "SEEN_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "p2pe_tokenization", "t": "PROTECTS", "b": "pin_pad"}, {"a": "p2pe_tokenization", "t": "PROTECTS", "b": "pos"}, {"a": "p2pe_tokenization", "t": "MITIGATES", "b": "pos_malware"}, {"a": "no_sad_storage", "t": "SEEN_IN", "b": "hall"}, {"a": "no_sad_storage", "t": "MITIGATES", "b": "pos_malware"}]}, "tool_used": "room_overview", "facts": "Room: Restaurant POS\nWhat it shows: Orders go from the POS to the kitchen display and cards are paid on encrypted terminals; card data is the most tightly regulated data here.\nKey lesson: Never store the CVV or PIN, mask card numbers, and treat unexpected emails on the POS PC with suspicion.\nDepartment based here: Food & Beverage (ext. 3100)\nSystems here: Point of Sale (POS), Card Payment Terminal, Email & Collaboration, Staff Laptops, PCs & Phones, Kitchen Display System\nThreats shown here: Phishing Email, POS Memory-Scraping Malware, Card Skimming & Terminal Tampering\nControls you can see: P2PE & Tokenization, Never Store CVV or PIN\nConcepts: Encryption vs Hashing, Cardholder Data Environment (PCI scope), Tokenization\nProcedures to know: Received a suspicious email, Clicked a phishing link or entered a password, A card terminal looks tampered with, The POS is down\nExits: Fireplace Close-up · Ordering Tablet (called 'Fireplace · Up Close' in the tour), Bar Inventory & ERP, Restaurant Close-up · POS Terminal (called 'Restaurant · Up Close' in the tour), Restaurant at Night · POS Down, Guest Arrival & Wi-Fi (called 'Lakeside Patio' in the tour)", "answer_stats": {"model": "qwen3.5:9b", "wall_s": 18.79, "load_s": 0.01, "prompt_tokens": 720, "prompt_s": 2.21, "gen_tokens": 121, "gen_s": 9.86, "tok_per_s": 12.3, "first_token_s": 8.93}}, "state": {}}

